cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use these measurements, cite this repository and the solver it measures.
title: interactor-tool-lbfgsb-bench
abstract: >-
  A host-native benchmark of the L-BFGS-B that contract-lbfgsb writes in Lean and
  emits through Slang (guest/drape/lbfgsb.cpp over vec_cpu.cpp, the Lean-emitted
  kernels on the CPU), against traditional bounded quasi-Newton solvers of the
  same type: LBFGSpp 0.3.0, the implementation the driver mirrors, and scipy's
  Fortran L-BFGS-B 3.0 (Byrd, Lu, Nocedal and Zhu).


  Eight bound-constrained problems, the five from contract-lbfgsb's own oracle
  generator plus a chained Rosenbrock at n=1000, a box QP at n=10000 and a
  logistic regression, are solved by all three solvers at two parameter settings
  (delta 1e-3 and 1e-10). The benchmark reports iterations, objective evaluations,
  wall time with the objective timed separately, and the objective and projected
  gradient at each stopping point, and gates the run on the driver reproducing
  LBFGSpp's work and result.
